      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hamburg%2C_Illinois",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The village once thrived as a river port where apples were shipped and banks buzzed with commerce.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hamburg%2C_Illinois",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Hamburg’s only public facility today is its post office, a quiet reminder of its past bustle.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hamburg%2C_Illinois",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A bluff monument marks the burial of riverboat captain Swarnes, who chose to rest upright overlooking the Mississippi.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hamburg%2C_Illinois",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "In 1975 National Geographic photographed the Delta Queen passing Hamburg, using Swarnes’ monument as a backdrop.",
